      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While a green juice packed with spinach and kale is very healthy, you need to be cautious with Vitamin K intake while taking warfarin. Many dark leafy greens, like spinach and kale, are high in Vitamin K, which can interfere with how warfarin works. It's best to maintain a consistent intake of these foods rather than drastically changing your amount one day to the next. Please discuss any significant dietary changes with your doctor or pharmacist to ensure your INR levels stay stable.",
